[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3421262864","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111835#issuecomment-3421262864","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111835","id":3421262864,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7L7FQQ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-20T09:39:54Z","updated_at":"2025-10-20T09:39:54Z","body":"Please describe this flickering, does the video flicker after changing scenes?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3421262864/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3421479488","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111835#issuecomment-3421479488","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111835","id":3421479488,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7L76JA","user":{"login":"seyondk","id":168323925,"node_id":"U_kgDOCghrVQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/168323925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk","html_url":"https://github.com/seyondk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-20T10:27:26Z","updated_at":"2025-10-20T10:27:26Z","body":"> Please describe this flickering, does the video flicker after changing scenes?\n\nYes, at the moment of switching scenes, the video will flash once(Black flashing). And even after I exported it, the problem still exists. Before 4.5, the switching was smooth. You can see the specific phenomenon in my video [flicker video.zip].","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3421479488/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3422290254","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111835#issuecomment-3422290254","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111835","id":3422290254,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7L_AFO","user":{"login":"berarma","id":162766,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mjc2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/162766?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma","html_url":"https://github.com/berarma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-20T14:19:11Z","updated_at":"2025-10-20T19:04:53Z","body":"I couldn't test the MRP yet, but it could be that setting the stream might be slower than before due to the length of the video being calculated. Taking the `set_stream` method out of the `_ready' method might solve it then. For example, by having the stream set before changing the scene.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3422290254/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3422302714","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111835#issuecomment-3422302714","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111835","id":3422302714,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7L_DH6","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-20T14:22:33Z","updated_at":"2025-10-20T14:22:33Z","body":"The scene is expected to be cleared when reloading, To ensure it displays something valid immediately I'd suggest adding a texture with a preview or the first frame etc. separately to ensure it renders correctly regardless of how fast it loads it\n\nHaven't tested the MRP yet because I'm not at my work computer but I'd also suggest using `preload` and a constant path for the clip to see if that speeds up loading","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3422302714/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3424712723","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111835#issuecomment-3424712723","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111835","id":3424712723,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MIPgT","user":{"login":"seyondk","id":168323925,"node_id":"U_kgDOCghrVQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/168323925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk","html_url":"https://github.com/seyondk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T05:18:48Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T05:27:46Z","body":"> The scene is expected to be cleared when reloading, To ensure it displays something valid immediately I'd suggest adding a texture with a preview or the first frame etc. separately to ensure it renders correctly regardless of how fast it loads it\n> \n> Haven't tested the MRP yet because I'm not at my work computer but I'd also suggest using `preload` and a constant path for the clip to see if that speeds up loading\n\nYes, thank you for providing ideas. Currently, after testing, it is indeed possible to use the first frame of the video as the background to solve the problem of switching flicker, but this is not a long-term solution. Simply using load or preload methods to load the scene in advance cannot solve the problem of flickering.\n\nThis has a significant impact on subsequent projects, as most of my current projects are in scenarios with multiple different trees, and the video playback is connected before and after, resulting in a poor flickering experience.\n\n<img width=\"911\" height=\"250\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e23e5275-0886-4215-a9a9-64bc294bd5de\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3424712723/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3424735406","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111835#issuecomment-3424735406","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111835","id":3424735406,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MIVCu","user":{"login":"seyondk","id":168323925,"node_id":"U_kgDOCghrVQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/168323925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk","html_url":"https://github.com/seyondk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T05:27:03Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T05:27:03Z","body":"> I couldn't test the MRP yet, but it could be that setting the stream might be slower than before due to the length of the video being calculated. Taking the `set_stream` method out of the `_ready' method might solve it then. For example, by having the stream set before changing the scene.\n\nYes, after the 4.5, I got the function of time, which is great. I easily created the function of playing progress bars.\n\nNow, the videos played in my scene1 and scene2 are the same file. I don't even use scripts, and setting Autoplay and Stream in the property panel of VideoStreamPlayer still causes this problem.\n\nIn the same scene, my video switching stream loading did not show any flickering during transitions.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3424735406/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3428003899","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111835#issuecomment-3428003899","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111835","id":3428003899,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MUzA7","user":{"login":"berarma","id":162766,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mjc2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/162766?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma","html_url":"https://github.com/berarma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T17:19:51Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T08:46:02Z","body":"After some testing, this is what I think is happening. VideoStreamPlayer uses the internal process notification to update its output. The internal process notification is skipped for one frame when changing the scene. Previous Godot versions would display the first video frame as soon as the `play` method was called, and this would result in the first video frame lasting longer than it should because only the deltas between internal process call updates were counted as video time. Since Godot 4.5, the video playback starts in the next internal process call to have a more consistent video playback frame rate from the first video frame, and thus the delay when changing the scene.\n\nThe old behavior in this case would be to show the first video frame immediately but frozen for the time it takes for the next internal process call to happen and catch up to the next video frame.\n\nIt would be something like this:\n\nGodot 4.4.1:\n\n- Change scene.\n- Play video, renders first video frame.\n- Godot renders frame.\n- Call to internal process, does nothing, still first video frame showing since the video time really starts now.\n- Godot renders frame.\n\nGodot 4.5:\n\n- Change scene.\n- Play video, no video frame yet.\n- Godot renders frame.\n- Call to internal process, displays first video frame, video time starts here.\n- Godot renders frame.\n\nNotice that in both cases the video time starts when internal process is called after calling `play` but in the former case the first video frame is already showing way before that.\n\nThe current behavior is more correct in terms of video playback but has that unfortunate side effect.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3428003899/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3430312647","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111835#issuecomment-3430312647","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111835","id":3430312647,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MdmrH","user":{"login":"seyondk","id":168323925,"node_id":"U_kgDOCghrVQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/168323925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk","html_url":"https://github.com/seyondk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seyondk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-22T03:02:20Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T03:03:02Z","body":"@berarma Thanks, berarma. I understand now that you said that. It should be the reason for the problem. Before Godot 4.5, I didn't actually notice the issue of incorrect playback time for the first frame. The short-term solution should be to use the first frame as the background for scene switching and see if there are any plans for optimization in the future. After all, if each video adds an image, the workload will increase slightly.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3430312647/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]